(6239045, 921370, 73564, '<td valign="top">thanks for the comments and fav''s.....I went to the basement, found everything there except the apples, they were grown on my property, though. :D I used an old crate, an old window, cigar box and jug. Happened to catch a shadow on the right edge of the window, to try to make it look realistic, bounced light from left.<br/> <br/>Oh and to the unchecked comment giver, I was not trying to make it look like anything from a mag..! I made this look as it did on my own, and I got it exactly how I pictured it. :)~<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-11-30 18:02:34.</i></td>', 'thanks for the comments and fav''s.....I went to the basement, found everything there except the apples, they were grown on my property, though. :D I used an old crate, an old window, cigar box and jug. Happened to catch a shadow on the right edge of the window, to try to make it look realistic, bounced light from left. Oh and to the unchecked comment giver, I was not trying to make it look like anything from a mag..! I made this look as it did on my own, and I got it exactly how I pictured it. :)~', '2010-11-30 17:59:48.000000', '2010-11-30 18:02:34.000000', 0),
(6239048, 921192, 101707, '<td valign="top">Wonderful film noir type image, and yes, very sexy. The grain works well here. Much under appreciated, should have scored higher.</td>', 'Wonderful film noir type image, and yes, very sexy. The grain works well here. Much under appreciated, should have scored higher.', '2010-11-30 18:06:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(6239054, 921206, 116649, '<td valign="top">You wouldn''t believe how many man-made objects were surrounding that wheel!  One more day extension, and I would have had the below snow-dusted photo that hid the grate, but you can see the boat dock, and the electrical pole.  If I adjusted the composition to block one thing, something else would show up, or the river wouldn''t be viewable at all!  Is I hal''f pressed my shutter so the light exposure would be correct at the river, I lost focus on the wheel!<br/> <br/>Live and learn.  Things to bring next time...   tripod instead of monopod, camouflage netting, manual focus, and a dusting of snow!  ;)<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=923051" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/115000-119999/116649/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_923051.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/115000-119999/116649/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_923051.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/115000-119999/116649/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_923051.jpg"/></a></td>', 'You wouldn''t believe how many man-made objects were surrounding that wheel!  One more day extension, and I would have had the below snow-dusted photo that hid the grate, but you can see the boat dock, and the electrical pole.  If I adjusted the composition to block one thing, something else would show up, or the river wouldn''t be viewable at all!  Is I hal''f pressed my shutter so the light exposure would be correct at the river, I lost focus on the wheel! Live and learn.  Things to bring next time...   tripod instead of monopod, camouflage netting, manual focus, and a dusting of snow!  ;)', '2010-11-30 18:12:55.000000', NULL, 0),
